      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's a revised version of the email:\n\nDear Marcus,\n\nI wanted to personally reach out to you regarding the Senior Developer position at our Austin office. We were truly impressed by your technical skills, particularly your expertise in backend development, which we believe would have been a valuable asset to our team. Unfortunately, after careful consideration, we have decided to move forward with another candidate whose experience aligns more closely with our specific cloud architecture needs.\n\nYour ability to design and implement scalable backend systems is impressive, and we were excited about the potential for you to contribute to our team's success. However, we have to prioritize the best fit for our team's current needs, and this other candidate's experience made them a stronger candidate for the role.\n\nI want to emphasize that this decision is final, and we appreciate the time and effort you invested in our interview process. We're grateful for the opportunity to have met you and appreciate your interest in joining our team. Your passion for backend development and problem-solving is evident, and we wish you the best of luck in finding a role that leverages your skills and experience.\n\nBest regards,\n[Your Name]\n\nThis revised version aims to acknowledge Marcus's specific strengths in backend development and express appreciation for his skills and experience.",
